Q3. Value vs. String Comparison
a = 25
b = "25"

print(type(a))  # <class 'int'>
print(type(b))  # <class 'str'>
Explanation:
a is an integer (int), representing a numerical value that can be used in arithmetic operations. b is a string (str), representing a text sequence enclosed in quotes.
